<%# One row of /admin/entries, drawn several thousand times on one page -- so it is the
    entry's data and nothing else. The watch / edit / delete actions are not here: there is
    one set of them on the page, and entry-table moves it into whichever row is pointed at or
    focused, building its links from this row's id. Rendered per row they were seven of each
    row's sixteen elements, some 24,000 across the table, for controls only ever visible on
    one row at a time. The name cell is where they go, which is why it is the one with a
    class. %>
<tr id="<%= dom_id(entry) %>">
  <td class="et-name"><%= link_to entry.name, entry_path(entry) %></td>
  <td><%= entry.list.name %></td>
  <td><%= entry.media %></td>
  <td><%= "#{entry.length} min" if entry.length.to_i.positive? %></td>
  <td><%= entry.resolved_source&.name %></td>
  <td class="et-stream"><%= entry_stream_mark(entry.stream) %></td>
</tr>
